This is a working _non released_ CDROM, door that allows users to
list and download, Fred Fish files.  Not quite finished, but works fine
as is.

* NOTE *  For this door to work, your Fred Fish CDROM _MUST_ have the
          FishCat locator in the CDROM with this directory structure

          "cd0:locators/fishcat/index"

          Now as I was using an A500/A590 CDROM parnetted to the A3000, I had
          the following directory structure.

          "NET:cd0/locators/fishcat/index"

          So this means if you want to use an A590 parnetted to your current
          machine, the you don't need to recompile the source, assuming you
          have the correct Fred Fish disc.  But if you have a CDROM within
          your machine, then you'll have to change the "INDEX_FILE_IN"
          macro within "make_index.c", "FISH_DATA" macro within 
          "CDROM_Lister.c" and "FISH_DISKS" macro with "CDROM_Lister.c" 
          to the non Parnet path above. 

          With the correct Fred Fish CD and the correct re-building of the
          source, (to take into account whether you have a parnetted CDROM
          or not), you will then be able to build a new index file.

          Assuming you don't have a Fred Fish CD with the correct locator
          on it, (yeah I am a cheat, why build my own data base when
          some kind soul had already done it <evil grin>), then you'll 
          definitely be wanting to piss fart around with the source and
          you'll thus need to re-compile everything.
            

To compile the source, you'll need SAS C 6.X.

To install it, just use sumthin' akin to this:

  KEY  FUNCTION  EXTRAS  LOW  HIGH   PATH/FILENAME
   C      34       0     10   10000  DOORS:CDROM_Lister/CDROM_Lister

Then type make_index, and assuming you've fixed the paths in the two source
files, you will now have a freshly generated "cdrom.index" file within your
"DOORS:CDROM_Lister" directory, which the CDROM_Lister door will be able to
use. 


